 Anonymizes identifiers and literals in workload captures for sharing without exposing sensitive information.
 
+All SQL rewriting is performed on Materialize's own parsed AST by the `mz-sql-anonymize` helper binary, rather than by text substitution. This renames identifiers as whole tokens (no substring corruption or in-string rewrites) and redacts literals reliably. The parser is required: the anonymizer refuses to write output if the helper is missing or any statement fails to parse.
+
+**Building the helper:**
+```bash
+cargo build --release -p mz-sql-anonymize
+```
+The anonymizer locates the binary via the `MZ_SQL_ANONYMIZE_BIN` environment variable if set, otherwise in `target/release/` or `target/debug/`.
+
